Z||000000||MotherGoose||05-10-2000||09:40 AM||||Has anyone ever added a ram air system to there v-6.  Just like to know what you did,  and the pros and cons of doing it.||||reg||1
Z||000001||MotherGoose||05-10-2000||12:43 PM||||I guess no one has ever done it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||05-10-2000||01:02 PM||||Funny, I thought I had responded to this but didn't catch, Oh well, try it again....<P>I had a functional Ram Air system on my 87 4 cyl and was very pleased with it. It was easy since the air filter is so far "up wind" of the intake. I felt a difference (I won't say I got more hp) on passing power on the freeway. <P>I have only had partial success with my 85 GT. I have replaced the stock intake screen with a Holley type scoop (not the $177 one!) and replaced the airbox with a straight pipe. A little snug putting the fenderwell back in but it will fit. It just goes into the stock air intake etc. I did extensive engine work to it so I really don't know the difference in performance because of it. There are those who have put a straight pipe from the throttle body to a K&N filter just behind the intake panel. Not really RAM AIR, for the purists but probably just effective. The sound is all the differenece that I need. The K&N has a constant HISSSSSS even at idle where as my set up is a bit quieter but has a good hiss when accelerating. <BR>Hope this helps out. Hope this gets posted!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||MotherGoose||05-10-2000||01:08 PM||||Thanks for the Info<P>MotherGoose||||reg||1
